PATCH 460: deliverable #3 -- per-object render methods + render descriptor macros (the op-0x4c display-list
frontier).  Combines: (A) 22dd's cursor-bracket descriptor uVar1 = DAT_1000_d56a is carried as a 16-bit
truncation of the rebased host pointer (patch 325 typed d56a a pointer; patch 395 documents it as the
near-offset) -> g_mem-base-DEPENDENT (native lands on a valid struct, wasm on uninitialised) -> take the
DGROUP near offset (ptr - (g_mem+0x1c000)), base-independent.  (B) FUN_0000_29f4 threads 260c's published
m_260c_cf/m_260c_zf (Ghidra dropped them as in_CF/in_ZF=0 locals; patch-459 idiom).  (C) _DAT_1000_c724
macro: DGROUP:0x724 holds a near offset (024f writes it), not a stored host pointer -> rebase
g_mem+0x1c000+word[0x724].  (C2) 260c uses that rebased pointer directly.  (D/D2/D3) the per-object render/
display-list methods (c4df walk publishes the object in g_fist_render_si and record code in g_fist_render_dx
per patch 310, for the ARG-LESS __allregs dispatch) were reading STALE register params -> use the published
globals: c6e7 passes g_fist_render_si; ca2f/ca6b/c962 read g_fist_render_si for the object si; ca2f's record
header high byte = g_fist_render_dx.  RESULT: wasm cockpit-entry render divergence 1457->116 bytes (92%),
native mission-cockpit crop byte-matches the DOSBox oracle (AZER1, CYPRUS1 0-diff), menu/settings verify
flows pass.  asm-faithful to patch 310's published-globals design.
